@startuml google-auth-flow
title Google authentication from the client
hide footbox

actor User
participant "CRM client" as Client
participant "Google identity service" as Google
participant "CRM API" as Api

User -> Client: Choose Sign in with Google
Client -> Api: POST /api/auth/google/challenge
Api --> Client: 200 nonce and expiresAtUtc
Client -> Google: Start identity request with nonce
User -> Google: Choose a Google account
Google --> Client: Signed Google ID token with nonce
Client -> Api: POST /api/auth/google/sign-in\n{idToken, useNativeSession?}

alt Google subject linked to an active CRM account
    Api --> Client: 200 signedIn + CRM session
    Client --> User: Open CRM portal
else Verified email belongs to an active CRM account
    Api --> Client: 200 linkRequired + continuation token + verified email
    Client -> User: Ask user to authenticate to the matching CRM account
    User -> Client: Provide CRM password (email already provided)
    Client -> Api: Authenticate through CRM login
    Api --> Client: CRM session with access token
    User -> Client: Confirm linking
    Client -> Api: POST /api/auth/google/link\nCRM bearer token + continuation token
    Api --> Client: 204 No Content
    Client --> User: Continue with the current CRM session
else Verified email is new to CRM
    Api --> Client: 200 registrationRequired + continuation token
    Client -> User: Show Tutor or Student registration form
    User -> Client: Submit role and profile details
    Client -> Api: POST /api/auth/google/register\ncontinuation token + role + profile
    Api --> Client: 201 signedIn + CRM session
    Client --> User: Open CRM portal
end
@enduml
